      "text": "To convert a number from base 5 to base 10, we can use the formula:\n\n\\[\nN_{10} = a_n \\cdot 5^n + a_{n-1} \\cdot 5^{n-1} + \\cdots + a_1 \\cdot 5^1 + a_0 \\cdot 5^0\n\\]\n\nwhere \\( N_{10} \\) is the number in base 10, and \\( a_n, a_{n-1}, \\ldots, a_0 \\) are the digits of the number in base 5.\n\nFor the number \\( 3124_5 \\):\n- The digit \\( 4 \\) is in the \\( 0 \\)-th position, so:\n\\[\n4 \\cdot 5^0 = 4 \\cdot 1 = 4\n\\]\n\n- The digit \\( 2 \\) is in the \\( 1 \\)-st position, so:\n\\[\n2 \\cdot 5^1 = 2 \\cdot 5 = 10\n\\]\n\n- The digit \\( 1 \\) is in the \\( 2 \\)-nd position, so:\n\\[\n1 \\cdot 5^2 = 1 \\cdot 25 = 25\n\\]\n\n- The digit \\( 3 \\) is in the \\( 3 \\)-rd position, so:\n\\[\n3 \\cdot 5^3 = 3 \\cdot 125 = 375\n\\]\n\nAdding these values together:\n\\[\n4 + 10 + 25 + 375 = 414\n\\]\n\nSo, \\( 3124_5 = 414_{10} \\).\n\nFor the number \\( 3122_5 \\):\n- The digit \\( 2 \\) is in the \\( 0 \\)-th position, so:\n\\[\n2 \\cdot 5^0 = 2 \\cdot 1 = 2\n\\]\n\n- The digit \\( 2 \\) is in the \\( 1 \\)-st position, so:\n\\[\n2 \\cdot 5^1 = 2 \\cdot 5 = 10\n\\]\n\n- The digit \\( 1 \\) is in the \\( 2 \\)-nd position, so:\n\\[\n1 \\cdot 5^2 = 1 \\cdot 25 = 25\n\\]\n\n- The digit \\( 3 \\) is in the \\( 3 \\)-rd position, so:\n\\[\n3 \\cdot 5^3 = 3 \\cdot 125 = 375\n\\]\n\nAdding these values together:\n\\[\n2 + 10 + 25 + 375 = 412\n\\]\n\nSo, \\( 3122_5 = 412_{10} \\).\n\nFor the number \\( 124_5 \\):\n- The digit \\( 4 \\) is in the \\( 0 \\)-th position, so:\n\\[\n4 \\cdot 5^0 = 4 \\cdot 1 = 4\n\\]\n\n- The digit \\( 2 \\) is in the \\( 1 \\)-st position, so:\n\\[\n2 \\cdot 5^1 = 2 \\cdot 5 = 10\n\\]\n\n- The digit \\( 1 \\) is in the \\( 2 \\)-nd position, so:\n\\[\n1 \\cdot 5^2 = 1 \\cdot 25 = 25\n\\]\n\nAdding these values together:\n\\[\n4 + 10 + 25 = 43\n\\]\n\nSo, \\( 124_5 = 43_{10} \\).\n\nNow, we sum the values in base 10:\n\\[\n414 + 412 + 43 = 871\n\\]\n\nThus, the total dollar amount accumulated by the pirate is \\(\\boxed{871}\\).",
